      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pennville%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Originally called New Lisbon, the town was renamed Penn after William Penn when the post office adopted that name in 1839.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
